WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.430
(gentle music)

00:00:02.430 --> 00:00:03.330
- Check this out.

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:04.163
This is a map

00:00:04.163 --> 00:00:06.000
of some of the battery
manufacturing facilities

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.620
coming online in the US.

00:00:07.620 --> 00:00:10.110
And as you can see,
they're mostly over here.

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:12.030
See, as America tries to rapidly increase

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:13.860
its battery manufacturing capacity,

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:16.920
it's creating what some are
calling America's Battery Belt.

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:19.320
But the decisions around
where to build these factories

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:22.650
is moving America's automotive
heartland further South,

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:25.560
redistributing thousands
of jobs in the process.

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:26.760
So, what are the key factors

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:29.190
shaping where America's Battery Belt is?

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:30.023
Let's find out.

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:32.670
Okay, so first we need to explore

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:34.290
why so many battery factories

00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:35.880
are being built in America right now.

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:38.580
See, some battery factories
have been slowly coming online

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:39.810
in the US for years,

00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:41.880
but things stepped up
again when Biden signed

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:43.380
the Inflation Reduction Act,

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:46.080
which requires a certain
percentage of a vehicle's battery

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:47.580
be made in America

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.980
for it to qualify for federal incentives.

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:52.290
Spending on US battery
factories quadrupled

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:54.810
between 2019 and 2022,

00:00:54.810 --> 00:00:57.060
with some $70 billion of investments

00:00:57.060 --> 00:00:58.740
for batteries and auto manufacturing

00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:00.690
being announced over the last two years.

00:01:00.690 --> 00:01:03.420
And more than 15 new battery
factories or expansions

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:05.883
have been announced
since the start of 2021.

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:08.700
So, why are they mostly over here?

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:11.100
Well, given that batteries
are heavy things to ship,

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:13.290
the obvious place to
build battery factories

00:01:13.290 --> 00:01:16.080
may seem to be right next
to an automotive plant,

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:18.720
as proximity can reduce
transportation snarls.

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:21.120
That's partly why some
of the new factories

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:23.820
are in a similar area to
existing auto factories.

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:26.520
But proximity is far from the only factor

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:28.860
deciding where these factories should go,

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:31.230
as my colleague Nora Eckert
has been finding out.

00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:33.540
- The center of gravity
for the automotive industry

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:36.060
has traditionally been in the Midwest,

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:38.370
around Michigan specifically,

00:01:38.370 --> 00:01:41.700
and over time that has shifted
into the American South,

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:46.080
and that's been expedited
with this EV building boom.

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:48.150
- Nora has been chained to site selectors,

00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:49.680
essentially the people who decide

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:51.300
where these factories should go.

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:52.860
One key factory is connectivity

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:54.660
to transport networks like railways,

00:01:54.660 --> 00:01:57.450
which are far more prevalent
in the East of America.

00:01:57.450 --> 00:02:00.120
- For a battery plant or
for an EV assembly plant,

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:03.420
access to railway and ports is key.

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:04.950
- That may explain why these factories

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:06.540
are in the East of America,

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:07.830
but why the move South?

00:02:07.830 --> 00:02:10.350
- So, battery plants
and EV assembly plants

00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:11.940
require a lot of electricity,

00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:14.760
and more than your
traditional gas engine plant.

00:02:14.760 --> 00:02:18.030
So the lower electricity costs
in some areas of the South

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:19.380
compared to, say, Michigan,

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:21.900
make that a lot more
attractive for auto makers.

00:02:21.900 --> 00:02:24.540
- But perhaps the main factor
pushing these factories South

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:26.640
is whether the sites are turnkey,

00:02:26.640 --> 00:02:30.150
essentially, shovel-ready
sites with connected utilities

00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:32.340
just waiting to be developed on.

00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:34.800
- It's tough to build
up the facility itself

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:35.970
and bring in the workers,

00:02:35.970 --> 00:02:37.890
but as long as you've
got that base set up,

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:41.250
it becomes really attractive
for potential auto makers.

00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:44.070
- Georgia says it's spent
years prepping projects sites

00:02:44.070 --> 00:02:45.750
to attract car companies,

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:47.887
with its Commissioner for
Economic Development saying,

00:02:47.887 --> 00:02:50.430
"I feel like we are right
now riding that wave."

00:02:50.430 --> 00:02:53.910
All of that has been at about
2/3 of the new auto investment

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:55.560
announced over the past two years

00:02:55.560 --> 00:02:58.233
has gone down here to
sites in the US South.

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:01.830
So, what does this mean for
America's automotive heartland

00:03:01.830 --> 00:03:03.480
of Michigan and the Great Lakes?

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:06.420
- I think a big question for a
lot of people in the industry

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:07.890
is about Michigan's future

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:11.460
and if it's losing its power
in the automotive industry.

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:13.110
If anything, we're just
seeing the industry

00:03:13.110 --> 00:03:16.950
become a little more broadly
dispersed across the US

00:03:16.950 --> 00:03:19.650
instead of localized just
in the Michigan area.

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:21.990
- But even with this
race to build factories,

00:03:21.990 --> 00:03:24.030
the shift won't happen overnight.

00:03:24.030 --> 00:03:25.530
That's because as early movers

00:03:25.530 --> 00:03:27.660
in US battery manufacturing have found,

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:30.540
it can take years to train
workers and adapt machinery

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:32.430
to get a factory fully operational.

00:03:32.430 --> 00:03:34.740
So even though the
groundwork is being laid now,

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:36.300
it still might take a few years

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:38.463
for America's Battery Belt to truly form.

00:03:39.343 --> 00:03:41.850
(gentle music)

